# Competitive Template Audit: VST Plugin Development Playbooks

## Existing Playbook Analysis

### VST Plugin Playbook v7 (Unified) — `/home/myuser/agents/juce-agent/playbooks/vst-plugin-playbook-v7-unified.json`

**What it covers:**
- 13-phase development workflow (Phase 0-12)
- DSP implementation with sound design integration
- Audio thread safety patterns
- Parameter management (APVTS)
- Testing frameworks (Catch2, pluginval)
- CI/CD for cross-platform builds
- Prevention rules from real failure modes
- Knowledge base integration (Technical, Sound Design)

**What it does well:**
- Battle-tested phase structure from real projects (CogVST, Epiphany Machine)
- Detailed prevention rules with specific failure mode IDs
- Clear task ownership (human vs AI)
- Phase gates with explicit PASS/FAIL conditions
- Integration with Sound Design KB for creative-to-technical translation
- Session boundary recommendations

**What it misses:**
- **Commercial distribution** — No coverage of licensing, marketplaces, pricing
- **Marketing strategy** — No pre-launch, launch, post-launch activities
- **Business planning** — No revenue model, cost analysis, break-even calculations
- **Market research** — No competitive analysis, positioning guidance
- **Plugin beyond development** — Ends at Phase 12 (release prep), no distribution guidance

